// ── PHRASAL / predicative comparative OPERATORS (D63 §8.12, d63-comparative-phrasal.md §5) ──
// Closed-class function words over the scale category `cat_measure` (⟦·⟧ = Entity→float) / any `cat_n`.
// The SCALE SOURCE (measure nouns, gradable adjectives) is content-word data — importer-emitted or demo
// scaffolding, NOT here. `than`/`cat_pp_than` (above) supplies the standard. (Moved from the demo lexicon
// in B1; #9 cardinality then closes at scale over existing `cat_n` with no importer emission.)
// (6b) `greater` — degree-MORE over a MEASURE noun (noun/object frame); sem `λμ.λV.λy.λx. gt(μ(x),μ(y))`.
