// (6d′) `N-fold fewer` / `N-fold more` — the count comparatives with a FACTOR (D95 slice 9, decision 2),
// consumed on the left after the noun: `0.56-fold fewer deletion mutations than typical lineages` →
// `And(gt(card(T, y), card(T, x)), fold_lower(0.56, card(T, x), card(T, y)))`. The order is the plain
// comparative's own term, since every reading of `N-fold fewer` agrees on it; the factor is kept as
// written in the opaque `fold_lower`. The senses are the plain entries' own, so the ranker is not
// asked to choose between the two.
