// (6e′) ELIDED-`than` is a GRAMMAR SHIFT, not a lexical entry (D63 §8.12;
// d63-single-skeleton-defects.md). "more/less X" with no `than` is complete on its own: the comparative
// `((S[adj]\NP)/cat_pp_than)/cat_measure` above takes its measure to `(S[adj]\NP)/cat_pp_than`, and the
// `elided_than` unary shift (kernel: dcg::rules::constructions + the UnaryKind::ElidedThan table entry)
// saturates the pending `cat_pp_than` standard with the anaphoric placeholder `lexicon:anaphor` (→ an
// OPEN parse the D64 resolver fills — the elided comparison target). One general rule over any
// `X/cat_pp_than` REPLACES the former per-word `more_deg_bare`/`less_deg_bare` entries; the explicit
// `than_marker` still supplies an overt standard for "more X than Y". (`than [PP]` — the RELATUM
// standard "more dependent on WRN than on MSI" — is a separate two-measure relational-comparative slice,
// not a `than` widening; see kernel/tests/comparative_than.rs.)

// ── Argument-PP markers: prepositions as VERB/ADJECTIVE-subcategorized oblique complements ──
// "contributes TO cancers", "results FROM X", "dependent ON WRN", "associated WITH Z": the head
// *requires* the PP. The marker consumes the object NP and yields a `cat_pp_arg(prep)` (⟦·⟧ = Entity),
// transparently exposing the object (`λy. y`); a subcategorizing verb `(S\NP) / cat_pp_arg(any)` or a
// gloss-governed adjective `cat_measure / cat_pp_arg(prep_on)` binds it. A distinct `cat_pp_arg` (not a
// bare NP) FORCES the preposition — a plain transitive verb `(S\NP)/NP` (e.g. `affect`) cannot absorb
// `to X`. The **Prep feature** (D63 §5.3 C3-precision) tags each marker with its preposition, so a
// governed adjective selects the RIGHT one: `dependent` (prep_on) composes with `on` but not `to`
// (`*dependent to`). These are IN ADDITION to each preposition's VP-adjunct + noun-modifier entries
// above (the argument reading is a third parse, selected only by a subcategorizing head). There is
// one per `lexicon:Prep` constructor but the wildcard (`dcg::category::GOVERNED_PREPOSITIONS`).
resource lexicon:argmarker_sem : lexicon:SemTerm {
    lexicon:term = type_expr( ( fun (y : lexicon:Entity) => y : lexicon:Entity -> lexicon:Entity ) );
}
resource lexicon:to_arg : lexicon:LexicalEntry {
    core:description = "grammatical: preposition marking a goal or recipient, or the infinitival marker ('lead to death', 'to test').";
    lexicon:form     = "to";
    lexicon:cat      = type_expr( lexicon:fwd(lexicon:m_all, lexicon:cat_pp_arg(lexicon:prep_to), lexicon:cat_np(lexicon:Entity, lexicon:num_any)) );
    lexicon:sem      = lexicon:argmarker_sem;
    lexicon:sem_type = type_expr( lexicon:Entity -> lexicon:Entity );
    lexicon:sense    = "to";
}
resource lexicon:from_arg : lexicon:LexicalEntry {
    core:description = "grammatical: preposition marking origin or source ('arise from mutations').";
    lexicon:form     = "from";
